WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.703
The CrestApps Report Builder lets the people who run your site build their

00:00:05.703 --> 00:00:09.525
own reports by dragging fields, instead of writing queries.

00:00:09.525 --> 00:00:13.581
This video shows why it exists, how to build, chart and share a

00:00:13.581 --> 00:00:18.520
report, how to join data sets and reuse views, and every data source it reads.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.346
Your site keeps its data in many places:

00:00:26.346 --> 00:00:34.760
content items, users and roles, contact center calls, omnichannel activities, AI chat sessions, and text messages.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:39.572
Built-in reports answer the questions someone thought of in advance.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:43.360
A new question used to mean asking a developer for a new query.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:47.160
And the Report Builder is not limited to those.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:51.707
More data sources keep being added, and developers can plug in their own,

00:00:51.707 --> 00:00:54.930
so reports can cover any data your site can reach.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:00.202
The Report Builder puts the answer in the hands of the people asking.

00:01:00.202 --> 00:01:05.810
They pick data sets, join them, group and total them, add charts, and share the result.

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:15.368
A data source is the data of one module, such as Contents or Contact Center.

00:01:15.368 --> 00:01:21.510
Each source offers data sets, such as Activities or Users, and each data set has fields.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:28.642
A report combines data sets, picks columns and filters, and shows the result in visuals:

00:01:28.642 --> 00:01:32.240
tables, charts, metric strips and pivot tables.

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:35.803
A view is a saved, reusable data set.

00:01:35.803 --> 00:01:41.820
Other reports use its columns like any other fields, and it can refresh on a schedule.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:44.852
Everything respects permissions.

00:01:44.852 --> 00:01:48.937
A data source shows only what the person may read, and a saved

00:01:48.937 --> 00:01:51.760
report runs with the access of its owner.

00:01:55.940 --> 00:02:00.415
Turn on the Report Builder feature under Tools, Features.

00:02:00.415 --> 00:02:04.320
The Reports (OpenXml) feature adds Excel exports.

00:02:04.774 --> 00:02:08.921
The Report Builder appears under Reports in the admin menu.

00:02:08.921 --> 00:02:11.537
It lists every report you can open.

00:02:11.537 --> 00:02:14.345
Search them, or filter them by status:

00:02:14.345 --> 00:02:16.514
published, or not published.

00:02:16.966 --> 00:02:19.827
From the list, run a report or edit it.

00:02:19.827 --> 00:02:24.340
The Actions menu clones a report into your own copy, which is not

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:26.946
shared with anybody, or deletes it.

00:02:31.137 --> 00:02:32.776
Click New report.

00:02:32.776 --> 00:02:35.057
The builder has four tabs:

00:02:35.057 --> 00:02:38.407
Settings, Design, Data model and Sharing.

00:02:38.859 --> 00:02:43.203
On the Settings tab, give the report a title, a description and a

00:02:43.203 --> 00:02:49.199
category, and choose whether it appears in the admin menu and whether viewers may export it.

00:02:49.652 --> 00:02:52.435
On the Design tab, add a data set.

00:02:52.435 --> 00:02:58.072
The list groups the data sets by source; pick Activities, from Omnichannel.

00:02:58.523 --> 00:03:01.073
Its fields appear in the Data pane.

00:03:01.073 --> 00:03:05.863
Drag a field onto Columns, and the preview shows the result right away.

00:03:06.314 --> 00:03:08.822
Add Number of rows to count them.

00:03:08.822 --> 00:03:13.195
With a count, the report groups the rows by its other columns:

00:03:13.195 --> 00:03:16.154
here, activities per channel and status.

00:03:16.606 --> 00:03:20.765
A new report starts filtered on the last thirty days of its main

00:03:20.765 --> 00:03:24.151
date, which keeps reports over a lot of data quick.

00:03:24.151 --> 00:03:26.706
You can change or remove that filter.

00:03:30.898 --> 00:03:34.322
Click a column to edit it under Properties.

00:03:34.322 --> 00:03:39.074
An aggregate turns a number into a sum, an average, a count, a

00:03:39.074 --> 00:03:42.918
distinct count, a minimum, a maximum or a median.

00:03:43.371 --> 00:03:46.676
A transform changes a value before grouping.

00:03:46.676 --> 00:03:50.906
For a date, pick the day, the week, the month or the year,

00:03:50.906 --> 00:03:53.021
to see activity over time.

00:03:53.473 --> 00:03:56.282
Give each column a header and a format.

00:03:56.282 --> 00:04:01.775
The question mark lists common formats, such as one decimal place or a percentage.

00:04:01.775 --> 00:04:06.333
Hide a column from tables while keeping it for grouping and charts.

00:04:06.784 --> 00:04:12.852
Calculated fields use formulas, with functions for text, numbers, dates and aggregates.

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:15.331
This one is the completion rate:

00:04:15.331 --> 00:04:18.854
the completed activities divided by all of them.

00:04:19.305 --> 00:04:24.585
Drag the calculated field onto Columns, and it works like any other field.

00:04:28.786 --> 00:04:30.842
Drag a field onto Filters.

00:04:30.842 --> 00:04:34.184
A row filter narrows the data before grouping.

00:04:34.184 --> 00:04:39.776
A result filter applies after it, such as channels with more than ten activities.

00:04:40.228 --> 00:04:44.307
Let viewers change this filter, and pick how they choose:

00:04:44.307 --> 00:04:49.227
a drop-down list, a list with several choices, a recent period, a date

00:04:49.227 --> 00:04:51.558
or number range, or yes or no.

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:57.137
Exposed filters appear above the report, as searchable lists filled with the values

00:04:57.137 --> 00:04:58.520
found in the data.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.940
Viewers pick values and click Apply.

00:05:05.129 --> 00:05:09.246
Visuals are listed under Visuals, in the order they appear.

00:05:09.246 --> 00:05:12.349
A table shows the rows, and can add totals.

00:05:12.801 --> 00:05:15.633
Add a chart, and pick its type:

00:05:15.633 --> 00:05:19.842
bar, horizontal bar, line, area, pie or doughnut.

00:05:19.842 --> 00:05:23.821
Then pick the category and the values to plot.

00:05:24.509 --> 00:05:28.709
A metric strip shows a few key numbers at the top of the report.

00:05:29.161 --> 00:05:33.494
A pivot table puts one column down the side and spreads the values

00:05:33.494 --> 00:05:35.421
of another across the top.

00:05:35.871 --> 00:05:40.043
Set the width of each visual to place them side by side.

00:05:40.043 --> 00:05:46.571
Charts, metrics and totals regroup the underlying rows, so an average stays a true average.

00:05:50.771 --> 00:05:54.160
A join puts the rows of two data sets side by side.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:58.559
Each activity, for example, sits next to the user it is assigned to:

00:05:58.559 --> 00:06:02.601
the activity's Assigned to column is matched to the user's ID.

00:06:03.351 --> 00:06:06.157
Which rows stay depends on the join type.

00:06:06.157 --> 00:06:10.037
An inner join keeps only the rows that match on both sides:

00:06:10.037 --> 00:06:12.306
the activities that have a user.

00:06:12.306 --> 00:06:14.933
A left join keeps all the rows before:

00:06:14.933 --> 00:06:19.171
every activity, with the user's columns empty when there is none.

00:06:19.921 --> 00:06:23.913
A right join keeps all the rows of the joined data set:

00:06:23.913 --> 00:06:26.924
every user, even one without activities.

00:06:26.924 --> 00:06:30.261
A full join keeps all the rows of both sides.

00:06:31.861 --> 00:06:33.504
Add a second data set:

00:06:33.504 --> 00:06:34.208
Users.

00:06:34.208 --> 00:06:38.314
An activity refers to the user it is assigned to, so the builder

00:06:38.314 --> 00:06:39.781
joins them for you.

00:06:40.232 --> 00:06:42.261
Drag User name onto Columns.

00:06:42.261 --> 00:06:44.828
The activities are counted per agent.

00:06:44.828 --> 00:06:49.246
The builder joins them with an inner join, which keeps only the rows

00:06:49.246 --> 00:06:54.082
that match on both sides, so activities nobody is assigned to are left out.

00:06:54.535 --> 00:06:58.849
The Data model tab draws the data sets and how they are joined.

00:06:58.849 --> 00:07:00.850
The first one is the base.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:04.665
Each line is a join, and its badge shows the join type.

00:07:05.117 --> 00:07:07.157
Click the badge to change it.

00:07:07.157 --> 00:07:10.888
Make it a left join, to keep all the rows before, and back

00:07:10.888 --> 00:07:16.017
on the Design tab, the activities without an agent are counted too, with no agent.

00:07:16.472 --> 00:07:20.684
To join two data sets yourself, drag a column of one onto the

00:07:20.684 --> 00:07:22.885
matching column of the other:

00:07:22.885 --> 00:07:27.035
here, the campaign of an activity onto the ID of a campaign.

00:07:27.035 --> 00:07:30.682
Key columns are marked with a key, and listed first.

00:07:31.134 --> 00:07:34.030
A join can match on several columns.

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:40.304
Add matching columns adds another pair, and rows match only when every pair is equal.

00:07:44.492 --> 00:07:46.588
A report can be only data.

00:07:46.588 --> 00:07:53.662
This campaign summary is a plain table, with viewer filters, a calculated completion rate, and totals.

00:07:54.115 --> 00:07:56.821
A report can combine charts and data.

00:07:56.821 --> 00:08:00.786
This one shows a metric strip, a bar chart and a table of

00:08:00.786 --> 00:08:02.925
activity outcomes per agent.

00:08:03.376 --> 00:08:05.660
Tables can show subtotals.

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:11.085
With Role, Agent and Status, there is a subtotal for each agent within

00:08:11.085 --> 00:08:14.726
a role, one for each role, and a grand total.

00:08:15.176 --> 00:08:20.046
Pie charts and pivot tables suit shares and cross-tabs, such as the share

00:08:20.046 --> 00:08:23.436
of each disposition, and dispositions by channel.

00:08:27.637 --> 00:08:32.882
Contents offers one data set per content type, with its parts and fields.

00:08:32.882 --> 00:08:39.587
Owners, content pickers and user pickers reference other data sets, so they join automatically.

00:08:40.038 --> 00:08:44.033
Users offers the accounts of the site and their roles.

00:08:44.033 --> 00:08:48.028
Passwords, tokens and other secrets are never exposed.

00:08:48.479 --> 00:08:54.991
Contact Center offers interactions, call sessions and their quality, queues and queue items,

00:08:54.991 --> 00:08:59.709
agent profiles and sessions, callbacks, voicemail and recordings.

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:05.875
Omnichannel offers activities, dispositions, campaigns and activity batches.

00:09:05.875 --> 00:09:11.730
AI Chat offers chat sessions, and Messaging offers conversations and messages.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:16.189
The views you build are data sets too, and so are saved queries,

00:09:16.189 --> 00:09:18.309
when the Queries feature is on.

00:09:18.309 --> 00:09:20.600
Modules can add their own sources.

00:09:24.777 --> 00:09:27.896
Every change is saved in a draft as you work.

00:09:27.896 --> 00:09:33.157
Close the page and come back later, and the builder picks up where you left off.

00:09:33.607 --> 00:09:38.320
Click Publish to make the changes live for everybody who can open the report.

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:40.307
Each publish keeps a version.

00:09:40.759 --> 00:09:43.531
Versions lists every published version.

00:09:43.531 --> 00:09:45.565
Preview one, or restore it.

00:09:45.565 --> 00:09:50.124
When two people edit the same report, the builder shows who else has

00:09:50.124 --> 00:09:54.129
it open, and stops one from silently overwriting the other.

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:02.097
A view prepares a data set once, for many reports:

00:10:02.097 --> 00:10:06.470
its joins, calculated fields and filters live in one place.

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:08.488
Report Views lists them.

00:10:08.488 --> 00:10:09.900
Click Add View.

00:10:10.351 --> 00:10:12.029
Build it like a report.

00:10:12.029 --> 00:10:15.963
This one holds activities with the agent they are assigned to:

00:10:15.963 --> 00:10:20.591
add Activities, then Users, and make their join a left join, so activities

00:10:20.591 --> 00:10:22.211
without an agent stay.

00:10:27.066 --> 00:10:29.913
Add a calculated field for the agent:

00:10:29.913 --> 00:10:33.620
the user's name, or Unassigned when there is none.

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:36.136
Check the formula, and apply it.

00:10:39.042 --> 00:10:42.253
Then drag the columns that reports need:

00:10:42.253 --> 00:10:46.722
the activity's ID, the agent, the channel, and the status.

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:53.160
On the Settings tab, name the view, and choose when it refreshes.

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:56.279
Live runs it each time a report reads it.

00:10:56.279 --> 00:11:01.851
A schedule, such as every hour, stores the result, so reports read it quickly.

00:11:01.851 --> 00:11:02.780
Save it.

00:11:03.231 --> 00:11:05.328
Now build a report on it.

00:11:05.328 --> 00:11:06.749
Add a data set:

00:11:06.749 --> 00:11:09.251
the view is under Report views.

00:11:10.099 --> 00:11:15.182
Its columns are fields like any others, with the agent already worked out.

00:11:15.182 --> 00:11:19.629
Drag Agent, and Number of rows to count each agent's activities.

00:11:20.141 --> 00:11:25.567
Add a chart, and the report shows each agent's workload, without repeating the

00:11:25.567 --> 00:11:27.246
join or the formula.

00:11:27.246 --> 00:11:30.411
Every report built on the view reuses them.

00:11:34.627 --> 00:11:39.086
On the Sharing tab, share the report with people, and with roles.

00:11:39.086 --> 00:11:41.661
The Anonymous role makes it public:

00:11:41.661 --> 00:11:44.487
everyone can open it, signed in or not.

00:11:44.941 --> 00:11:48.647
A share link sends the report to people of the site, who open

00:11:48.647 --> 00:11:49.974
it once signed in.

00:11:49.974 --> 00:11:54.289
Pick the recipients, and choose when the link expires and how many times

00:11:54.289 --> 00:11:55.451
it can be used.

00:11:55.902 --> 00:12:00.752
Create the link, then copy it and send it, or let the site email it.

00:12:00.752 --> 00:12:04.882
Every link is listed, and you can revoke one at any time.

00:12:05.335 --> 00:12:10.835
A shared report reads data with your access, so share only what its viewers should see.

00:12:11.289 --> 00:12:16.169
Viewers run the report, change its filters, and export it as a CSV

00:12:16.169 --> 00:12:18.609
file, or as an Excel workbook.

00:12:22.809 --> 00:12:28.022
Developers add a data source by implementing Orchard Core's IDataSource.

00:12:28.022 --> 00:12:31.764
Its name, display name and description are static.

00:12:31.764 --> 00:12:37.979
It lists its data sets, describes their fields, and streams the rows a report asks for.

00:12:38.729 --> 00:12:46.682
For data kept in records, derive from RecordDataSource and RecordDataSet, and register the source with AddDataSource.

00:12:46.682 --> 00:12:50.109
The data set decides what each person may read.

00:12:52.109 --> 00:12:56.757
The Report Builder turns the data of your site into reports that anyone

00:12:56.757 --> 00:12:58.749
can build, chart and share.

00:12:58.749 --> 00:13:00.319
Thanks for watching.

